statement.paragraph:
Let $$A = \,\,\begin{bmatrix}
    1 & 0 & 2 \\
    2 & 1 & 6 \\
    {- 3} & 0 & 5
    \end{bmatrix} \,{and} B = \,\begin{bmatrix}
    4 & 3 & 2 & 7 \\
    2 & {- 9} & 3 & {- 4}
    \end{bmatrix}.$$

If the vectors $\mathbf{a}_{1} = \,\,\begin{bmatrix}
    1 \\
    3 \\
    1
    \end{bmatrix}$, $\mathbf{a}_{2} = \,\,\begin{bmatrix}
    5 \\
    3 \\
    {- 1}
    \end{bmatrix}$, and $\mathbf{a}_{3} = \,\,\begin{bmatrix}
    0 \\
    2 \\
    0
    \end{bmatrix}$ represent the columns of a matrix $A$, write out the matrix $A$.
